  "api_error_status": null,
  "result": "I fixed the 100x charge for Japan and Korea, and `npm test` passes with 9 of 9 tests. The new regression tests fail without the fix: 3 failed, 6 passed, with the `src` change stashed.\n\n**Root cause:** `buildChargePayload` in `src/payments/gateway/payload.js` lower-cases the currency (`\"jpy\"`) for the gateway and then passes that lower-case code to `toMinor`. The currency registry only had upper-case keys, so the lookup for `\"jpy\"` found nothing. It then fell back to the default exponent of 2, so ¥1,500 became 150,000. USD and EUR use exponent 2 anyway, so they were never affected. KRW, VND, CLP, BHD and KWD were affected the same way.\n\n**Fix:** In `src/lib/currency/registry.js`, `exponent`, `isSupported` and `symbol` now ignore case and whitespace. That fixes this payload and protects any other caller that passes a lower-case code.\n\n**Tests:** I added three tests to `test/charge.test.js`:\n- JPY ¥1,500 is charged as 1500.\n- KRW ₩12,000 is charged as 12000.\n- KWD 1.5 is charged as 1500, which checks a three-decimal currency.\n\nThere is also an untracked `eval/` directory in the repo that I didn't create or touch.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
